  "reviewed_by": "Claude Code (operator task: stop per-tool-call workspace provenance hashing from stalling chats)",
  "reason": "run_project_tool_hooks now records a tool.before provenance baseline only when a discovered hook subscribes to tool.after (also for tool.after-only hooks, which previously always got tool_baseline_is_missing); a before-only hook gets an unsupported no_tool_after_hook receipt and Core hashes nothing, and a denied call no longer re-snapshots. snapshot() reuses per-process SHA-256 fingerprints keyed by path+dev+inode+size+mtime_ns+ctime_ns, so repeated snapshots read only changed files and a timed-out snapshot keeps its progress. Selected: all of test_workspace_provenance.py (incl. two new fingerprint-reuse tests), test_native_hooks.py, and the tool-hook/provenance tests in test_automation_runtime.py (incl. two new before-only/after-only regressions).",
  "exclusions": "test_workspace_provenance.py::test_large_unchanged_checkout_shares_chunks_and_queries_only_compact_index fails identically on origin/main (AsyncSession has no attribute 'query', async-storage test rot) and is left out. No UI, native or Playwright change; docs/WORKSPACE_PROVENANCE.md is not part of the product knowledge index. test_automation_runtime.py::test_inherited_shared_search_hook_enforces_real_host_run_command_and_process_io needs the protected Nebula memory runner service, which CI runners lack (MemoryEnforcementUnavailable); it passes locally where the runner is installed.",
